{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And when Moses came before YHWH, etc.</b> When the matter was being spoken with Moses, or when Moses himself was speaking with Israel, he did not put the veil over his face, because of 'and your eyes shall see your teacher.' And 'your teacher' implies from the Holy One, blessed be He, to Moses, and from Moses to Israel. But when he was not standing before the Holy One, blessed be He, and was not speaking with Israel, then he would put the veil, as it is written, 'and Moses returned the veil' — so that they would not constantly see the sanctity of the radiance of his face, and he would appear to them as ordinary. For it was from the radiance of the Shekhinah, and also so that their eyes would not feast upon the radiance of the Shekhinah." "<b>Mask.</b> From the root of sotah, and it has no root-form other than soh. Good — the passage of parashat Ki Tissa."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {1 "The cryptic final phrase 'שלימא סדרא דפרשת כי תשא' appears to be a copyist's or typesetter's note indicating that the section/order of parashat Ki Tissa is complete (Aramaic שלימא = 'it is complete/finished'); translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:00.883537787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}